{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,145p' results/ideas/02_exact_refit_contender_screening/program_1/src/program.py; sed -n '220,340p' results/ideas/02_exact_refit_contender_screening/program_1/src/program.py; sed -n '831,873p' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '769,816p' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '940,1005p' task/evaluate_final.py; cat .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json 2>/dev/null || cat scientific-evidence/schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json; find .codex/skills -name validate_claims.py; python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('references_provenance.json'));print(p.keys());print(json.dumps(p['references'][0],indent=2))\ns=json.load(open('paper_strategy.json'));print('TITLE',s['recommended_title']);print('PLAN',s['figure_plan']);print('RATIONALE',s['narrative_rationale'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,145p' results/ideas/02_exact_refit_contender_screening/program_1/src/program.py; sed -n '220,340p' results/ideas/02_exact_refit_contender_screening/program_1/src/program.py; sed -n '831,873p' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '769,816p' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '940,1005p' task/evaluate_final.py; cat .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json 2>/dev/null || cat scientific-evidence/schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json; find .codex/skills -name validate_claims.py; python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('references_provenance.json'));print(p.keys());print(json.dumps(p['references'][0],indent=2))\ns=json.load(open('paper_strategy.json'));print('TITLE',s['recommended_title']);print('PLAN',s['figure_plan']);print('RATIONALE',s['narrative_rationale'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"CPU influence-guided comparison deletion; finite JSON handle(request) protocol.\n\nEvery request is a dict with op below. Responses have EXACTLY the documented\nkeys; no additional fields. No paths or external state are accepted or returned.\nAll seeds are arbitrary nonnegative integers; they select RNG, never workload.\n\nreset {seed:int} -> {ok:true}: clear ALL buffers, certificates and tokens.\nexport_chunk {token:str,index:int} -> {error:'unknown_token'} for unknown tokens,\nor {data:str(base64)} for a live output token and valid zero-based chunk index.\nThis same operation probes stale exported state immediately after each reset.\nimport_start {n_rows:int<=100000,n_players:int in [2,256],regularization:float>0,\n dtype:'<f8',shape:[n_rows,4],encoding:'base64',byte_order:'little',\n nbytes:int<=67108864,chunks:int in [1,8]} -> {ok:true}.\nIt replaces the input staging buffer, not RNG; no solve before commit.\nimport_chunk {index:int,data:str(base64)} -> {ok:true}: ordered chunks, each\nat most 8388608 decoded bytes. No shared files. At most 128 MiB staging.\nimport_commit {} -> {ok:true}: validate byte count and decode C-order float64\nrows [participant_a,participant_b,observed_a_win_fraction,row_key]. Endpoints\nare distinct integers in [0,n_players), outcomes are 0,0.5,1; keys are unique\nnonnegative exact integers <=2**53. Rows are observed analysis inputs, not\nhidden prediction labels. n_players, regularization and row count configure\nworkload independently of seed. No scores or references are supplied.\nsolve {fractions:[0.001,0.005,0.01],max_iterations:100} -> {ok:true}.\nFit mean pair logloss + regularization/2 * sum(theta**2), zero-sum theta.\nChoose any clean nonleader contender, solve H direction=e_leader-e_contender,\ninfluence_i=(sigmoid(theta_a-theta_b)-outcome_i)*(direction_a-direction_b).\nSort ascending influence rounded to 10 decimals, then ascending stable row key.\nRank participants by descending logits rounded to 8 decimals, then ascending\ninteger identity. Deletion sets must\nbe nested EXACT prefixes of this order at floor(fraction*n_rows) budgets.\nChanging contender is allowed; undisclosed post-selection refinement is not.\nThe exported certificate is UTF-8 finite JSON with exactly theta:[m floats],\ncontender:int, direction:[m floats], influence:[n floats], deletions:[3 lists\nof integer row keys]. Evaluator recomputes residuals, selection and refits;\nthese numbers are untrusted certificates, never scores or validity flags.\nexport_start {} -> {token:str<=80 ASCII,nbytes:int<=67108864,chunks:int<=8,\n encoding:'base64',dtype:'json',shape:[],byte_order:'none'}; output divided\ninto fixed 8388608-byte chunks (last may be shorter).\nrelease {} -> {ok:true}: erase input staging; keep exported state live until\nnext reset so stale-state tests can exercise the actual exported data.\n\nEach JSON request/response including envelope/framing must be <64 MiB. Maximum\nlogical input/output is 64 MiB, at most 8 chunks; wire chunks are ~10.7 MiB.\nNo candidate timing/state-change report is requested. No scoring feedback is\ngiven. Native CLI is JSON-lines for local debugging; production uses handle.\n\nContender screening is deterministic and uses only the clean fit. For every\nnonleader, construct its required influence order and three exact prefixes.\nUsing the clean Hessian, predict the full score displacement for each prefix,\nincluding the mean-loss regularization correction. Shortlist at most six,\nincluding the screening winner and clean runner-up. Compare their frozen\nprefixes using converged retained-data mean-loss ridge refits. Maximize the sum\nof original-leader rank drops, target reversals, and clipped gap closure, then\nprefer clean rank. Failed or incomplete candidates are excluded; if none remain,\nuse the screening winner. Refit scores stay internal. Export only clean-fit\ncertificates, never refine an order, and never infer metadata from row keys.\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport math\nimport sys\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.linalg import cho_factor, cho_solve\nfrom scipy.special import expit\n\nSTATE = {}\nCHUNK = 8 * 1024 * 1024\n\n\ndef fit(rows, players, regularization, iterations):\n    first = rows[:, 0].astype(int)\n    second = rows[:, 1].astype(int)\n    outcome = rows[:, 2]\n    pair_index = first * players + second\n    pair_counts = np.bincount(pair_index, minlength=players * players)\n    pair_wins = np.bincount(pair_index, weights=outcome, minlength=players * players)\n    theta, hessian = fit_aggregates(pair_counts, pair_wins, regularization,\n                                    iterations=iterations, return_hessian=True)\n    return theta, hessian, pair_counts, pair_wins\n\n\ndef fit_aggregates(retained_counts, retained_wins, regularization,\n                   initial_theta=None, iterations=100, return_hessian=False):\n    players = math.isqrt(len(retained_counts))\n    retained_rows = int(retained_counts.sum())\n    if retained_rows <= 0:\n        raise RuntimeError('No retained comparisons')\n    observed = np.flatnonzero(retained_counts)\n    first, second = observed // players, observed % players\n    retained_counts, retained_wins = retained_counts[observed], retained_wins[observed]\n    scores = np.zeros(players) if initial_theta is None else initial_theta.copy()\n    scores -= np.mean(scores)\n\n    def quantities(scores):\n        margin = scores[first] - scores[second]\n        probability = expit(margin)\n        pair_residual = (retained_counts * probability - retained_wins) / retained_rows\n        data_gradient = np.bincount(first, pair_residual, minlength=players) - np.bincount(second, pair_residual, minlength=players)\n        gradient = data_gradient + regularization * scores\n        weight = retained_counts * probability * (1 - probability) / retained_rows\n        hessian = np.diag(np.bincount(first, weight, minlength=players) + np.bincount(second, weight, minlength=players) + regularization)\n        np.add.at(hessian, (first, second), -weight)\n        np.add.at(hessian, (second, first), -weight)\n        data_loss = np.sum(retained_counts * np.logaddexp(0, margin) - retained_wins * margin)\n        objective = data_loss / retained_rows + 0.5 * regularization * np.dot(scores, scores)\n        return objective, gradient, hessian\n\n    for iteration in range(iterations):\n        objective, gradient, hessian = quantities(scores)\n        if np.max(np.abs(gradient)) < 1e-11:\n            break\n        step = cho_solve(cho_factor(hessian, lower=True, check_finite=False), gradient, check_finite=False)\n        rate = 1.0\n        for attempt in range(30):\n            trial = scores - rate * step\n            trial -= np.mean(trial)\n            trial_objective, trial_gradient, unused_hessian = quantities(trial)\n            sufficient_decrease = trial_objective <= objective - 1e-4 * rate * np.dot(gradient, step)\n            roundoff_descent = trial_objective <= objective + 8 * np.finfo(float).eps * max(1.0, abs(objective)) and np.max(np.abs(trial_gradient)) < np.max(np.abs(gradient))\n            if sufficient_decrease or roundoff_descent:\n                scores = trial\n                break\n            rate *= 0.5\n        else:\n            break\n    unused_objective, gradient, hessian = quantities(scores)\n    if not np.isfinite(gradient).all():\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Bradley-Terry fit did not converge\")\n    if not np.isfinite(scores).all() or np.max(np.abs(gradient)) > 1e-9:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Bradley-Terry fit did not converge\")\n    if return_hessian:\n        return scores, hessian\n    return scores\n\n\ndef shortlist_contenders(screen_records, incumbent_contender, runner_up, limit=6):\n    shortlist = []\n    ordered = [incumbent_contender, runner_up]\n    ordered.extend(record['contender'] for record in sorted(screen_records, key=lambda record: record['score'], reverse=True))\n    for contender in ordered:\n        if contender not in shortlist:\n            shortlist.append(contender)\n        if len(shortlist) >= limit:\n        removed_wins = np.zeros_like(pair_wins)\n        previous_budget = 0\n        warm_theta = theta\n        rank_drop_sum = 0\n        target_reversals = 0\n        gap_closure_sum = 0.0\n        original_gap = theta[leader] - theta[contender]\n        complete = True\n        for budget in budgets:\n            removed = order[previous_budget:budget]\n            removed_counts += np.bincount(pair_index[removed], minlength=players * players)\n            removed_wins += np.bincount(pair_index[removed], weights=rows[removed, 2], minlength=players * players)\n            previous_budget = budget\n            cache_key = tuple(sorted(order[:budget].tolist()))\n            if cache_key not in refit_cache:\n                try:\n                    refit_cache[cache_key] = refit_prefix(pair_counts, pair_wins, removed_counts,\n                                                         removed_wins, regularization, warm_theta)\n                except (RuntimeError, np.linalg.LinAlgError, ValueError, FloatingPointError):\n                    refit_cache[cache_key] = None\n            trial_theta = refit_cache[cache_key]\n            if trial_theta is None:\n                complete = False\n                break\n            warm_theta = trial_theta\n            trial_ranking = np.lexsort((np.arange(players), -np.round(trial_theta, 8)))\n            rank_drop_sum += int(np.flatnonzero(trial_ranking == leader)[0])\n            trial_gap = trial_theta[leader] - trial_theta[contender]\n            target_reversals += int(trial_gap < -1e-8)\n            gap_closure_sum += float(np.clip((original_gap - trial_gap) / max(original_gap, 1e-8), 0.0, 2.0))\n        if complete:\n            clean_rank = clean_ranks[contender]\n            candidate_score = (rank_drop_sum, target_reversals, gap_closure_sum, -clean_rank)\n            exact_candidates.append({'score': candidate_score, 'selection': selection})\n    if not exact_candidates:\n        return incumbent_selection\n    selected = max(exact_candidates, key=lambda candidate: candidate[\"score\"])\n    return selected['selection']\n\n\ndef handle(request):\n    operation = request['op']\n    if operation == 'reset':\n        if type(request['seed']) is not int or request['seed'] < 0:\n            raise ValueError('invalid seed')\n        STATE.clear()\n        STATE['rng'] = np.random.default_rng(request['seed'])\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'export_chunk':\n        if request['token'] != STATE.get('token'):\n            return {'error': 'unknown_token'}\n        index = request['index']\n        if type(index) is not int or not 0 <= index < math.ceil(len(STATE['output']) / CHUNK):\n            raise ValueError('invalid chunk index')\n        return {'data': base64.b64encode(STATE['output'][index*CHUNK:(index+1)*CHUNK]).decode('ascii')}\n    if operation == 'import_start':\n        count, players = request['n_rows'], request['n_players']\n        if not (type(count) is int and 1 <= count <= 100000 and type(players) is int and 2 <= players <= 256):\n            raise ValueError('invalid shape')\n        if (request['dtype'], request['shape'], request['encoding'], request['byte_order'],request['nbytes']) != ('<f8',[count,4],'base64','little',count*32):\n            raise ValueError('invalid input metadata')\n        if type(request['chunks']) is not int or not math.ceil(count*32/CHUNK)<=request['chunks']<=8:\n            raise ValueError('invalid chunk count')\n        if not 0 < request['regularization'] <= 1:\n            raise ValueError('invalid regularization')\n        STATE.update(metadata=request, staging=bytearray(), next_chunk=0)\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'import_chunk':\n        if request['index'] != STATE['next_chunk'] or STATE['next_chunk']>=STATE['metadata']['chunks']:\n            raise ValueError('unordered chunk')\n        chunk = base64.b64decode(request['data'], validate=True)\n        if len(chunk)>CHUNK or len(STATE['staging'])+len(chunk)>STATE['metadata']['nbytes']:\n            raise ValueError('oversize chunk')\n        STATE['staging'].extend(chunk)\n        STATE['next_chunk'] += 1\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'import_commit':\n        metadata = STATE['metadata']\n        if len(STATE['staging']) != metadata['nbytes'] or STATE['next_chunk'] != metadata['chunks']:\n            raise ValueError('incomplete input')\n        rows = np.frombuffer(STATE['staging'], dtype='<f8').reshape(metadata['shape']).copy()\n        if not np.isfinite(rows).all():\n            raise ValueError('nonfinite input')\n        STATE['rows'] = rows\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'solve':\n        if request['fractions'] != [0.001,0.005,0.01] or request['max_iterations'] != 100:\n            raise ValueError('invalid solve settings')\n        rows = STATE['rows']; metadata = STATE['metadata']\n        theta, hessian, pair_counts, pair_wins = fit(rows, metadata['n_players'], metadata['regularization'], request['max_iterations'])\n        fractions = request['fractions']\n        contender, direction, influence, order = select_contender(rows, theta, hessian, metadata['regularization'], fractions, pair_counts, pair_wins)\n        budgets = [int(fraction * len(rows)) for fraction in fractions]\n        deletions = [[int(key) for key in rows[order[:budget], 3]] for budget in budgets]\n        result = {\"theta\": theta.tolist(), \"contender\": int(contender), \"direction\": direction.tolist(), \"influence\": influence.tolist(), \"deletions\": deletions}\n        output = json.dumps(result,allow_nan=False,separators=(',',':')).encode()\n        if len(output)>64*1024*1024:\n            raise ValueError('oversize output')\n        STATE['output'] = output\n        STATE['token'] = hashlib.sha256(output).hexdigest()\n        return {'ok':True}\n    if operation == 'export_start':\n        return {'token':STATE['token'],'nbytes':len(STATE['output']),'chunks':math.ceil(len(STATE['output'])/CHUNK),\n                'encoding':'base64','dtype':'json','shape':[],'byte_order':'none'}\n    if operation == 'release':\n        for key in ('rows','staging','metadata','next_chunk'):\n            STATE.pop(key,None)\n        return {'ok':True}\n    raise ValueError('unknown operation')\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    for line in sys.stdin:\n        print(json.dumps(handle(json.loads(line)),allow_nan=False,separators=(',',':')),flush=True)\ndef final_uncertainty(outcomes,episodes,datasets,deadline,smoke):\n    bootstrap = np.random.default_rng(709237)\n    seeds = list(dict.fromkeys(episode['seed'] for episode in episodes))\n    intervals = {}\n    for name,short in [('paired_gain_vs_random','random'),('paired_gain_vs_disagreement','disagreement')]:\n        means = [sum(outcomes[index][name] for index,episode in enumerate(episodes) if episode['seed']==seed)/4 for seed in seeds]\n        samples = bootstrap.choice(means,size=(8 if smoke else 256,len(seeds)),replace=True).mean(axis=1)\n        intervals['paired_gain_'+short+'_ci_low'] = float(np.quantile(samples,.025))\n        intervals['paired_gain_'+short+'_ci_high'] = float(np.quantile(samples,.975))\n    group_results = {}\n    valid = True\n    for family in ('arena','nba'):\n        index = next(index for index,episode in enumerate(episodes) if episode['family']==family and not episode['permuted'])\n        solution = outcomes[index]['solution']\n        rows,players,groups = datasets[family]\n        unique,inverse = np.unique(groups,return_inverse=True)\n        records = []\n        for repetition in range(2 if smoke else 32):\n            result = {'candidate':0.,'random':1.,'disagreement':1.,'gain_random':-1.,'gain_disagreement':-1.,'complete':False}\n            if solution is not None:\n                weights = np.bincount(bootstrap.integers(0,len(unique),size=len(unique)),minlength=len(unique))[inverse].astype(float)\n                try:\n                    clean = trusted_fit(rows,players,deadline,weights)\n                    for method in ('candidate','random','disagreement'):\n                        scores = []\n                        for mask in solution[method+'_masks']:\n                            retained = weights.copy(); retained[np.isin(rows[:,3],mask)] = 0\n                            fitted = trusted_fit(rows,players,deadline,retained)\n                            scores.append(disruption(clean,fitted)[0])\n                        result[method] = sum(scores)/3\n                    result['gain_random'] = result['candidate']-result['random']\n                    result['gain_disagreement'] = result['candidate']-result['disagreement']\n                    result['complete'] = True\n                except (TimeoutError,RuntimeError):\n                    result.update(candidate=0.,random=1.,disagreement=1.,gain_random=-1.,gain_disagreement=-1.,complete=False)\n                    valid = False\n            else:\n                valid = False\n            records.append(result)\n        group_results[family] = records\n    return intervals,group_results,valid\n\n\ndef load_data(smoke):\n    root = pathlib.Path(os.environ.get('TASK_SOURCE_DIR',pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent))/'resources'/PLANE\n    datasets = {}\n    for family in ('arena','nba'):\n        manifest = json.loads((root/(family+'_manifest.json')).read_text())\n        raw = (root/(family+'.json')).read_bytes()\n        if hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()!=manifest['payload_sha256'] or manifest['plane']!=PLANE:\n            raise ValueError('resource integrity failed')\n        payload = json.loads(raw)\n        if manifest['cross_plane_content_intersection']!=0 or manifest['cross_plane_source_id_intersection']!=0:\n            raise ValueError('content split audit failed')\n        for record in payload['provenance']:\n            code = hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(['split-v1-20261027',family,record['group']],ensure_ascii=False,sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':')).encode()).hexdigest()\n            if (int(code,16)%100<30)!=(PLANE=='search'):\n                raise ValueError('split membership failed')\n        rows = np.array(payload['rows'],dtype=np.float64)\n        groups = np.array([record['group'] for record in payload['provenance']])\n        players = len(payload['participants'])\n        if smoke:\n            exposure = np.bincount(rows[:,:2].astype(int).ravel(),minlength=players)\n            selected = [int(np.argmax(exposure))]\n            while len(selected)<min(12,players):\n                neighbor = np.isin(rows[:,0],selected)^np.isin(rows[:,1],selected)\n                candidates = np.bincount(rows[neighbor,:2].astype(int).ravel(),minlength=players)\n                candidates[selected] = -1\n                if candidates.max()<=0:\n                    break\n                selected.append(int(np.argmax(candidates)))\n            selected = sorted(selected)\n            keep = np.isin(rows[:,0],selected)&np.isin(rows[:,1],selected)\n            rows,groups = rows[keep][:1024],groups[keep][:1024]\n            mapping = {old:new for new,old in enumerate(selected)}\n            rows[:,0] = [mapping[int(value)] for value in rows[:,0]]\n            rows[:,1] = [mapping[int(value)] for value in rows[:,1]]\n            players = len(selected)\n        if not 2<=players<=256 or not 100<=len(rows)<=100000 or len(set(rows[:,3]))!=len(rows):\n            raise ValueError('invalid observed data shape')\n        datasets[family] = (rows,players,groups)\n    return datasets\n\n\nMETRICS = ['combined_score','random_baseline_score','disagreement_baseline_score','paired_gain_vs_random',\n           'paired_gain_vs_disagreement','mean_leader_rank_drop','control_pass_rate','completion_rate','correct']\nif PLANE=='final':\n    METRICS += ['paired_gain_random_ci_low','paired_gain_random_ci_high','paired_gain_disagreement_ci_low','paired_gain_disagreement_ci_high']\n\n\ndef worst_case(episode):\n            if np.max(np.abs(constant_gradient))>2e-7:\n                constant = {'theta':[0.]*players,'contender':int(ranking(clean)[1]),'direction':[0.]*players,\n                            'influence':[0.]*len(rows),'deletions':[[],[],[]]}\n                try:\n                    validate_certificate(constant,canonical,players,clean)\n                except ScientificInvalid:\n                    controls[1] = True\n            method_masks = {}\n            curves = {}; leader_curves = {}\n            rng = np.random.default_rng(episode['seed'])\n            random_order = rng.permutation(len(canonical))\n            margins = design@clean\n            losses = np.logaddexp(0,margins)-canonical[:,2]*margins\n            disagreement_order = np.lexsort((canonical[:,3],-losses))\n            orders = {'random':random_order,'disagreement':disagreement_order}\n            for method_index,method in enumerate(('random','disagreement','copy','candidate')):\n                method_deadline = reserved_method_deadline(now=time.monotonic(),episode_deadline=deadline,methods_remaining=3-method_index,work_seconds=method_work,cleanup_seconds=.6)\n                with time_bound(method_deadline):\n                    if method=='candidate':\n                        value,previous_token = solve_candidate(call,rows,players,previous_token)\n                        try:\n                            theta,masks = validate_certificate(value,rows,players,clean)\n                        except (TypeError,ValueError,IndexError,OverflowError) as error:\n                            raise ProtocolError('malformed certificate') from error\n                        controls[2] = True\n                    elif method=='copy':\n                        masks = [[],[],[]]\n                    else:\n                        masks = [[int(key) for key in canonical[orders[method][:int(fraction*len(canonical))],3]] for fraction in FRACTIONS]\n                    method_masks[method] = masks\n                    scores = []; drops = []\n                    for mask in masks:\n                        retained = canonical[~np.isin(canonical[:,3],mask)]\n                        if method=='candidate':\n                            try:\n                                fitted = trusted_fit(retained,players,method_deadline)\n                            except RuntimeError as error:\n                                raise ProtocolError('candidate perturbation refit invalid') from error\n                        else:\n                            fitted = baseline_fit(retained,method_deadline)\n                        score,drop = disruption(clean,fitted)\n                        scores.append(score); drops.append(drop)\n                    curves[method] = scores; leader_curves[method] = drops\n            controls[0] = curves['copy']==[0.,0.,0.] and leader_curves['copy']==[0.,0.,0.]\n            key = (episode['seed'],episode['family'])\n            if not episode['permuted']:\n                matched[key] = {'theta':theta,'masks':method_masks['candidate'],'curves':curves['candidate']}\n            else:\n                reference = matched.get(key)\n                controls[3] = reference is not None and bool(np.max(np.abs(theta-reference['theta']))<2e-5) and all(set(first)==set(second) for first,second in zip(method_masks['candidate'],reference['masks'])) and bool(np.max(np.abs(np.array(curves['candidate'])-reference['curves']))<1e-8)\n            result = worst_case(episode)\n            result.update(combined_score=sum(curves['candidate'])/3,random_baseline_score=sum(curves['random'])/3,\n                disagreement_baseline_score=sum(curves['disagreement'])/3,\n                paired_gain_vs_random=sum(first-second for first,second in zip(curves['candidate'],curves['random']))/3,\n                paired_gain_vs_disagreement=sum(first-second for first,second in zip(curves['candidate'],curves['disagreement']))/3,\n                mean_leader_rank_drop=sum(leader_curves['candidate'])/3,completion_rate=1.,controls=controls,duration=time.monotonic()-begin,\n                solution={'family':episode['family'],'permuted':episode['permuted'],'curves':curves,'candidate_masks':method_masks['candidate'],\n                          'random_masks':method_masks['random'],'disagreement_masks':method_masks['disagreement'],'clean_scores':clean.tolist()})\n            return result\n        def record_episode_failure(failure):\n            record_failure(failure)\n            try:\n                client.close(failed=True)\n            except (OSError,RuntimeError,TimeoutError):\n                if PLANE=='search':\n                    print('cleanup_failure component=candidate category=cleanup_failure operation=cleanup',file=sys.stderr)\n{\n  \"$id\": \"https://schemas.agentic-scientist.local/scientific-evidence/artifact-manifest.schema.json\",\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"artifact\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"id\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"kind\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"source\",\n            \"derived\",\n            \"manuscript\",\n            \"figure\",\n            \"table\",\n            \"script\",\n            \"log\",\n            \"other\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"media_type\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"path\": {\n          \"description\": \"Path to the artifact relative to the scientific-evidence root when possible.\",\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"sha256\": {\n          \"description\": \"Optional hash recorded when the producing workflow computes one.\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"path\",\n        \"kind\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"derived_from\": {\n      \"description\": \"Inline @evidence refs or stable ids describing the artifact inputs.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"minLength\": 1,\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"generated_by\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"command\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"minLength\": 1,\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"cwd\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"finished_at\": {\n          \"format\": \"date-time\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"script_path\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"script_sha256\": {\n          \"pattern\": \"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"started_at\": {\n          \"format\": \"date-time\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"script_path\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"named_outputs\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"type\": [\n          \"string\",\n          \"number\",\n          \"integer\",\n          \"boolean\",\n          \"array\",\n          \"object\",\n          \"null\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"description\": \"Optional machine-readable outputs emitted by the derivation.\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"notes\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"schema_name\": {\n      \"const\": \"scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"schema_name\",\n    \"artifact\",\n    \"derived_from\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Scientific Evidence Artifact Manifest\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py\ndict_keys(['campaign_results_dir', 'count', 'generated_at', 'queries', 'reference_query_plan', 'references', 'results_dir'])\n{\n  \"citation_count\": 4914,\n  \"citation_key\": \"Bradley1952RANKAO\",\n  \"id\": \"ref.s2.7d47ee5f84103529f84297c98c21dadb4742e3ff\",\n  \"paper_id\": \"7d47ee5f84103529f84297c98c21dadb4742e3ff\",\n  \"query\": \"\\\"Rank Analysis of Incomplete Block Designs: I. The Method of Paired Comparisons\\\"\",\n  \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-11-17T22:32:49.162071+00:00\",\n  \"source_url\": \"https://api.semanticscholar.org/graph/v1/paper/7d47ee5f84103529f84297c98c21dadb4742e3ff?fields=paperId%2Ctitle%2Cyear%2Cvenue%2CcitationCount%2CcitationStyles%2Curl\",\n  \"title\": \"RANK ANALYSIS OF INCOMPLETE BLOCK DESIGNS THE METHOD OF PAIRED COMPARISONS\",\n  \"venue\": \"\",\n  \"year\": 1952\n}\nTITLE Exact-Refit Audits of Pairwise Ranking Sensitivity\nPLAN ['Figure 1: early six-block concept overview of two data settings, shared Bradley–Terry audit, frozen orders, bounded selection, independent refits, and conditional fixed-mask uncertainty.', 'Figure 2: two dataset panels of grouped dots at three deletion budgets, comparing normalized inversions across the studied selector, high-loss deletion, and random deletion.', 'Figure 3: two comparator panels showing all unique stored conditional bootstrap gains for Arena and NBA against zero; explicitly fixed masks and no reselection.']\nRATIONALE The strongest evidence is the direct final comparison on two real-data settings and its conditional uncertainty analysis, not an optimization success story. Use one common sensitivity question with condition-specific evidence blocks, not a causal test of evaluation design. The inspected implementation supports the mechanism description; evaluator refits support measured effectiveness. Search configurations are descriptive supporting material, not independently replicated final ablations. The paper is viable as a bounded empirical audit without universal superiority or novelty-priority claims.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
