{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_88","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/home/agent-home/.codex/tmp/arg0/codex-arg0xizKj9/apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: claims_grounding.json\n+{\n+  \\\"claims\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The final evaluation completed and was qualified; this does not establish generalization or universal method superiority.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.qualification.status\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.qualification.correct\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": []\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Final mean inversion fractions are 0.011722185737596697 for the studied selector, 0.009340217174121283 for high-loss deletion, and 0.003902759168170127 for random deletion (1.172%, 0.934%, and 0.390% after rounding).\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.metric.combined_score\\\", \\\"final.metric.disagreement_baseline_score\\\", \\\"final.metric.random_baseline_score\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": []\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Final aggregate paired disruption gains are 0.002381968563475412 against high-loss and 0.00781942656942657 against random deletion, or 0.238 and 0.782 percentage points rounded.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.metric.paired_gain_vs_disagreement\\\", \\\"final.metric.paired_gain_vs_random\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": []\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The studied selector's aggregate normalized original-leader rank drop is 0.03305066318764949; no comparator-specific leader-drop result is claimed.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.metric.mean_leader_rank_drop\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": []\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The final evidence covers Arena and NBA at three deletion budgets with five seeds and reversed-row controls, not additional expert- or model-judge tasks.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"locator\\\": \\\"/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes[*]/solution/cases\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The final clean-score vectors have 64 Arena and 74 NBA participants. Prefix lengths are Arena 38/190/381 and NBA 41/207/414.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"locator\\\": \\\"episodes[0].solution.cases: clean_scores lengths and candidate_masks lengths\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"At Arena budgets 0.1%, 0.5%, 1%, studied inversions are 0.005952380952380952/0.008432539682539682/0.008928571428571428; high-loss inversions are 0.001488095238095238/0.010416666666666666/0.01636904761904762. The high-loss comparator is more disruptive at the two larger budgets.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"locator\\\": \\\"episodes[*].solution.cases[family=arena,permuted=false].curves\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"At NBA budgets 0.1%, 0.5%, 1%, studied inversions are 0.011477230655312847/0.012587930396149574/0.022954461310625694; high-loss inversions are 0.0018511662347278786/0.009255831173639394/0.016660496112550906. The studied selector is more disruptive at all measured NBA budgets.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"locator\\\": \\\"episodes[*].solution.cases[family=nba,permuted=false].curves\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The random-curve means in Table 1 and Figure 2 are computed over the five unpermuted seed cases per dataset; the studied selector exceeds those means in every dataset-budget cell.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"derived_artifacts\\\": [\\\"analysis_summary.json\\\", \\\"results_table.tex\\\", \\\"figures/dataset_budget_comparison.pdf\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Studied and high-loss curves are deterministic across recorded seeds, all corresponding reversed-row method curves agree, and no-deletion curves are zero.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.control_pass_rate\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"locator\\\": \\\"episodes[*].solution.cases[*].curves and controls\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"There are 32 unique complete fixed-mask group-weight records per dataset; the same block is repeated identically in all five seed exports and is not counted as 160 independent draws.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"locator\\\": \\\"episodes[*].solution.conditional_group_bootstrap\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"All stored conditional high-loss-relative gains are negative in Arena and positive in NBA. Arena range/mean is [-0.7936507937,-0.2314814815]/-0.5042989418 pp; NBA range/mean is [0.2221399482,1.9498951006]/0.8056429717 pp.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"locator\\\": \\\"episodes[0].solution.conditional_group_bootstrap.{arena,nba}[*].gain_disagreement\\\",\n+      \\\"derived_artifacts\\\": [\\\"analysis_summary.json\\\", \\\"bootstrap_table.tex\\\", \\\"figures/conditional_resampling_contrasts.pdf\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Stored conditional random-relative gains range from -0.2149470899 to 0.4960317460 pp on Arena and 0.5923731951 to 2.2954461311 pp on NBA. These are stored ranges, not confidence bounds.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"locator\\\": \\\"episodes[0].solution.conditional_group_bootstrap.{arena,nba}[*].gain_random\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The final seed-resampling gain interval is [0.007377907506332164,0.008168732424939618] versus random; the high-loss-relative endpoints both equal 0.002381968563475412.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.metric.paired_gain_random_ci_low\\\", \\\"final.metric.paired_gain_random_ci_high\\\", \\\"final.metric.paired_gain_disagreement_ci_low\\\", \\\"final.metric.paired_gain_disagreement_ci_high\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": []\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Conditional group-weight uncertainty holds the first unpermuted masks fixed, refits weighted clean and deleted rankings, and does not repeat contender selection; weighted removed mass is not fixed by nominal row fraction.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"Efron1979\\\", \\\"Davison1997\\\", \\\"Field2007\\\", \\\"Owen2007\\\"],\n+      \\\"implementation_sources\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:831\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The evaluated objective is retained-mean logistic loss with centered scores, half-win ties, and quadratic ridge 0.001. All-pairs inversions and normalized leader drop are distinct endpoints.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"Bradley1952\\\", \\\"Davidson1970\\\", \\\"Kendall1938\\\"],\n+      \\\"implementation_sources\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:647\\\", \\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:680\\\", \\\"source_evidence/selector.py:84\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Clean-Hessian contrast influence defines immutable nested prefixes at fractions 0.001,0.005,0.01. The screening displacement includes the retained-mean regularization correction in Equation 4.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"Hampel1974\\\", \\\"Koh2017\\\", \\\"Giordano2019\\\", \\\"Broderick2020\\\"],\n+      \\\"implementation_sources\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/selector.py:145\\\", \\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:706\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Selection shortlists at most six contenders, retaining the screening maximizer and runner-up, compares exact retained fits by leader drops, target reversals below -1e-8, closure clipped to [0,2], and clean rank. Failed finalist fits are excluded, with fallback to the screening maximizer.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"implementation_sources\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/selector.py:138\\\", \\\"source_evidence/selector.py:145\\\", \\\"source_evidence/selector.py:231\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The selected implementation uses ordered-pair sufficient statistics, centered Newton updates, Cholesky solves, line search, warm starts and removed-set caching. The independent evaluator fits from zero with L-BFGS-B.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"implementation_sources\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/selector.py:70\\\", \\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:667\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"High-loss deletion orders descending clean logistic loss with stable-key tie resolution; random deletion uses seeded permutation prefixes and all deletion methods share budgets and independent refitting.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"implementation_sources\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:949\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Source-defined numerical settings, rounding rules, stationarity, contrast-solve, score-agreement and influence tolerances are those recorded in the supplementary methods; they are protocol settings, not performance measurements.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"implementation_sources\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/selector.py:84\\\", \\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:667\\\", \\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:680\\\", \\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:706\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The uncertainty source specifies seed 709237, 256 seed-mean resamples with .025/.975 quantiles, and 32 group-weight resamples per dataset; Figure 3 and the supplemental table retain the unique records only.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"implementation_sources\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:831\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Partition metadata records pinned sources, normalized content grouping, deterministic content splits, largest components, and the cross-partition overlap audit. Final row counts are 38192 Arena and 41418 NBA, with NBA 2898 rows excluded outside its retained component; these are protocol metadata rather than comparative performance results.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"Chiang2024\\\", \\\"NBAdata\\\"],\n+      \\\"implementation_sources\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/manifests/arena_manifest.json\\\", \\\"source_evidence/manifests/nba_manifest.json\\\", \\\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:769\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Descriptive development aggregate values are 0.013240276724865765 for clean-Hessian selection and 0.01595532053579999 for bounded exact refits and retained-curvature expansion. They are not final controlled ablations, equivalence tests, or runtime comparisons.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_03\\\", \\\"result.top_program_01\\\", \\\"result.top_program_02\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"implementation_sources\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/clean_hessian_selector.py\\\", \\\"source_evidence/expanded_selector.py\\\", \\\"source_evidence/selector.py\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The retained-curvature comparison configuration uses at most 24 proxy contenders and 12 exact finalists, preserving the bounded selector finalists; no causal attribution of its score is made.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_02\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"implementation_sources\\\": [\\\"source_evidence/expanded_selector.py:153\\\", \\\"source_evidence/expanded_selector.py:266\\\", \\\"source_evidence/expanded_selector.py:312\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Classical ranking, estimation, influence and bootstrap references supply context, not measurements of the evaluated configuration.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"ref.Zermelo1929\\\", \\\"ref.Thurstone1927\\\", \\\"ref.Bradley1952\\\", \\\"ref.Ford1957\\\", \\\"ref.Hunter2004\\\", \\\"ref.Turner2012\\\", \\\"ref.Davidson1970\\\", \\\"ref.Firth1993\\\", \\\"ref.Plackett1975\\\", \\\"ref.Negahban2012\\\", \\\"ref.Shah2017\\\", \\\"ref.Kendall1938\\\", \\\"ref.Hampel1974\\\", \\\"ref.Cook1977\\\", \\\"ref.Koh2017\\\", \\\"ref.Giordano2019\\\", \\\"ref.Broderick2020\\\", \\\"ref.Chiang2024\\\", \\\"ref.Min2025\\\", \\\"ref.NBAdata\\\", \\\"ref.Efron1979\\\", \\\"ref.Davison1997\\\", \\\"ref.Rubin1981\\\", \\\"ref.Field2007\\\", \\\"ref.Owen2007\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [\\\"Zermelo1929\\\", \\\"Thurstone1927\\\", \\\"Bradley1952\\\", \\\"Ford1957\\\", \\\"Hunter2004\\\", \\\"Turner2012\\\", \\\"Davidson1970\\\", \\\"Firth1993\\\", \\\"Plackett1975\\\", \\\"Negahban2012\\\", \\\"Shah2017\\\", \\\"Kendall1938\\\", \\\"Hampel1974\\\", \\\"Cook1977\\\", \\\"Koh2017\\\", \\\"Giordano2019\\\", \\\"Broderick2020\\\", \\\"Chiang2024\\\", \\\"Min2025\\\", \\\"NBAdata\\\", \\\"Efron1979\\\", \\\"Davison1997\\\", \\\"Rubin1981\\\", \\\"Field2007\\\", \\\"Owen2007\\\"]\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n*** Add File: REPRODUCIBILITY.md\n+# Reproduction and provenance\n+\n+## Scope and known gap\n+\n+This package regenerates all reported quantitative plots and tables from the sealed\n+observations in \"'`paper_data.json`. It contains readable evaluated selector and evaluator\n+snapshots under `source_evidence/`, including descriptive development comparators.\n+The workspace'\"'s \"'`task/resources/{search,final}` contains normalized observations and\n+manifests. The `task` and `results` links point to staged run artifacts, not public\n+repositories. Do not interpret those links as a complete standalone data release.\n+\n+A complete raw-source-to-normalized-partition builder and the original downloaded\n+archives were not staged. End-to-end raw reconstruction therefore remains incomplete.\n+The manuscript explicitly preserves this limitation. No new scientific evaluation,\n+optimizer experiment, bootstrap draw, or comparison condition was run during writing.\n+\n+## Environment\n+\n+The evaluated CPU analysis declares `numpy==2.2.6` and `scipy==1.15.3` in\n+`source_evidence/requirements.txt`. Use a Python environment with those requirements\n+for scientific reruns. The evaluator sets BLAS/OpenMP-related thread counts to two.\n+Its source requires Linux process isolation/resource controls and checks those controls;\n+do not remove them to obtain a nominally successful result.\n+\n+Manuscript plotting additionally needs matplotlib, Pillow, and NumPy. During writing,\n+auxiliary packages were installed in `/tmp/paper-tools`, outside the manuscript tree.\n+`paper-tools-versions.txt` records the actual installed manuscript-tool versions.\n+Compilation requires pdflatex, BibTeX, the installed LaTeX packages used in `paper.tex`,\n+and Poppler utilities for rendered validation. The selected local ICLR style has a\n+5.5-inch text width and 9-inch text height; no geometry settings were changed.\n+\n+## Public data acquisition\n+\n+Download originals to a private `data/` directory, not into a distributable code tree.\n+These commands specify the upstream inputs only; they do **not** replace the missing\n+normalization builder.\n+\n+```sh\n+mkdir -p data\n+curl -L --fail '\"\\\\\n+  https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmarena-ai/arena-human-preference-55k/resolve/18c298340948c0e7f7727399fd459cca6ce0ca6f/train.csv \\\\\n+  -o data/arena_train.csv\n+curl -L --fail \\\\\n+  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fivethirtyeight/data/4c1ff5e3aef1816ae04af63218015066e186c147/nba-elo/nbaallelo.csv \\\\\n+  -o data/nbaallelo.csv\n+sha256sum data/arena_train.csv data/nbaallelo.csv\n+\"'```\n+\n+Expected SHA-256 values are:\n+- Arena: `0692154aaf20fc6649090c3f49b6b5dd1e693a765ecb5f0856ae0da5946f5be2`\n+- NBA: `d46ed3540ee8d9eca31b3e94cc8c777e0be5156173d814ebf65b8195e8d616bc`\n+\n+Sources declare Apache-2.0 and CC-BY-4.0, respectively. Consult upstream terms before\n+redistributing data. The pinned NBA README was consulted at `literature/NBAdata.md`.\n+The manifests in `source_evidence/manifests/` record the original and normalized\n+payload hashes, normalization, grouping, component filtering, and overlap audit.\n+No source hash is offered as substantive support for an implementation claim.\n+\n+## Regenerate paper artifacts (no experimental rerun)\n+\n+```sh\n+python build_paper_artifacts.py\n+pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex\n+bibtex paper\n+pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex\n+pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex\n+```\n+\n+In the writing environment, invoke `/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python` for plotting.\n+The plotting command took seconds locally; elapsed values are recorded in\n+`paper_validation_report.json`, not presented as a scientific runtime comparison.\n+\n+Artifact mapping:\n+- Figure 1 (`figures/audit_overview.png`): synchronous concept-figure renderer owned\n+  by the parent workflow; the guarded placeholder is deliberately not a result plot.\n+  The plotting script never overwrites a completed render.\n+- Figure 2 (`figures/dataset_budget_comparison.{pdf,png}`):\n+  `build_paper_artifacts.py`, unpermuted final curves, random means over recorded seeds.\n+- Figure 3 (`figures/conditional_resampling_contrasts.{pdf,png}`): same script, one\n+  unique stored conditional group-weight block; display jitter seed 41.\n+- Table 1 (`results_table.tex`): same script, stored curves and floored mask lengths.\n+- Development table: direct registry values embedded in `paper.tex`, mapped in\n+  `claims_grounding.json` to the three development source IDs.\n+- Complete conditional table (`bootstrap_table.tex`): same script, stored gains\n+  converted to percentage points, without new resampling.\n+- `analysis_summary.json`: same extraction, including unrounded values.\n+\n+Quantitative PDFs remain vector graphics; PNG exports use 300 DPI. Adjacent provenance\n+sidecars link the derived artifacts to the immutable evidence registry and script.\n+\n+## Scientific rerun from staged normalized inputs (not executed during writing)\n+\n+```sh\n+TASK_SOURCE_DIR=\"$PWD/task\" AGENTIC_TASK_QUALIFICATION=1 '\"\\\\\n+  python source_evidence/evaluate_final.py \\\\\n+  --program_path \\\"\"'$PWD/source_evidence/selector.py\" '\"\\\\\n+  --results_dir /tmp/ranking-final-rerun\n+\"'```\n+\n+This command requires staged resources and the declared evaluator environment.\n+The evaluator internally uses seeds 1009, 2027, 4051, 8089, and 16127, with canonical\n+and reversed rows for both datasets. Its conditional uncertainty RNG seed is 709237;\n+the clean and high-loss procedures are deterministic. Wall limits are source-defined\n+limits, not measured expected runtime. The original final manifest records elapsed\n+evaluation time of about 208 seconds on the original environment; hardware portability\n+and rerun time have not been measured here. A writing-time rerun was deliberately not\n+performed. Scientific reruns must not overwrite `paper_data.json` or its final sources.\n+\n+## Literature access and exclusions\n+\n+Existing retrieval output contained irrelevant matches and duplicate records. It was\n+replaced by exactly identified foundational ranking, influence, and resampling works,\n+the explicitly allowed Arena/influence/removal/vote-rigging identities, and the pinned\n+NBA documentation. `references_provenance.json` records exact endpoints and consulted\n+local files. Where no abstract was available (Bradley--Terry, Zermelo, Kendall), only\n+the bibliographic record was consulted; no detailed external result is attributed to\n+these records. Other references were consulted at abstract or documentation level,\n+not claimed as fully read papers. A wrong DOI for Ford and one for Field were rejected\n+by title and resolved with exact-title queries. A guessed Maystre arXiv identifier\n+resolved to an unrelated spinor paper; its abstract was seen and excluded, and that\n+identity is not cited. The final bibliography uses the exactly identified Rank\n+Centrality work instead. The PMLR endpoint was unavailable. These were unrelated\n+identity mismatches, not encounters with the prohibited study. No prohibited-study\n+page was knowingly accessed, no title/authors/results of it were inferred, and no\n+citations, related-paper lists, or derivatives were traversed.\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+```sh\n+python .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py --tex paper.tex --bib references.bib\n+python .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py '\"\\\\\n+  --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json \\\\\n+  --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir .\n+python .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py --paper-dir .\n+bash .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh verify --root-dir .\n+bash .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh paper.tex\n+\"'```\n+\n+The last command additionally audits compilation inputs and rendered supplementary\n+content. `paper_validation_report.json` distinguishes successful checks from any\n+environment-specific tool limitation; no failed gate is represented as passed.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n/tmp/paper-tools/bin/pip freeze > paper-tools-versions.txt\npython .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py --tex paper.tex --bib references.bib\npython .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir . > /tmp/claim_validate.log 2>&1; tail -18 /tmp/claim_validate.log\npython .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py --paper-dir .'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
