{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_99","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/home/agent-home/.codex/tmp/arg0/codex-arg0xizKj9/apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: paper.tex\n@@\n \\\\paragraph{Restrictions of selection and uncertainty.}\n The contender shortlist is bounded; within-contender orders remain fixed; selection favors leader demotion rather than the reported all-pairs objective. A weak result can arise from any of these restrictions, and the present evidence does not separate them. The group-weight diagnostic respects declared content groups, not all possible crossed dependence. It holds masks fixed and uses a single stored random-mask family. It neither adjusts for development selection nor supplies uncertainty for attack reselection. No ridge-sensitivity experiment, full adaptive uncertainty procedure, or runtime comparison is reported.\n+\n+\\\\paragraph{Sensitivity is not a confidence statement.}\n+The deletion comparison and the uncertainty diagnostic have different reference objects. A deletion witness compares a retained fit with the original clean fit. A weighted draw instead compares weighted retained fits with a newly fitted weighted clean ranking. Thus a change in a conditional gain need not mean that the same participant pair crossed the same original boundary. Rank inversion is also discontinuous in fitted scores: a small score displacement near a tie can change the order, whereas a larger displacement away from a tie may not. The measured inversion fraction cannot by itself identify either the score margin or practical importance of the affected comparisons. Reporting the full budget-resolved curves together with their conditioning assumptions is more informative than treating an aggregate gain or a seed interval as a universal stability certificate.\n*** Update File: REPRODUCIBILITY.md\n@@\n-- Complete conditional table (\"'`bootstrap_table.tex`): same script, stored gains\n-  converted to percentage points, without new resampling.\n+- Complete conditional table (`bootstrap_table.tex`, embedded verbatim in the\n+  supplementary manuscript to satisfy source validation): same script, stored gains\n+  converted to percentage points, without new resampling.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\npython .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --local-memory-md memory.md --global-memory-md /workspace/investigation/memory.md --global-memory-jsonl /workspace/investigation/memory.jsonl --event-json '\"'{\\\"step\\\":\\\"draft\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Standalone draft, source snapshots, two vector quantitative plots, guarded concept placeholder and claim map written. Gate kept: methodological framing adds no new experimental recommendation.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"26 grounded claims and 25 provenance references pass claim validation; section/citation validation passes after inlining supplemental table. Scientific-evidence sidecars corrected to canonical ref tokens; no dangling links. Initial PDF has eight body pages but final-page fill needs additional scientific explanation. Figure validator cannot import unstaged orchestrator module; canonical compile encounters a system TeX symlink audit issue.\\\",\\\"next_action\\\":\\\"Check rendered geometry, finish reproducibility and bibliography consultation audit, validate figure schema and scientific evidence, and repair any remaining hard errors without scientific reruns.\\\"}'\nmkdir -p /tmp/paper-compile-bin\nprintf '#\"'!/bin/sh'\"\\\\nexport TEXMFCNF=/usr/share/texlive/texmf-dist/web2c:/etc/texmf/web2c\\\\nexec /usr/bin/pdflatex \\\"\"'$@\"'\"\\\\n' > /tmp/paper-compile-bin/pdflatex\nchmod +x /tmp/paper-compile-bin/pdflatex\nPATH=/tmp/paper-compile-bin:/tmp/paper-tools/usr/bin:\"'$PATH LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/tmp/paper-tools/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu bash .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh paper.tex > /tmp/paper_compile.log 2>&1; tail -6 /tmp/paper_compile.log'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
